s="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="138">Good question — here’s the short distinction between the <strong data-start="57" data-end="79">two retro variants</strong> you could choose for your upgraded <code data-start="115" data-end="127">index.html</code> aesthetic:</p>
<hr data-start="140" data-end="143">
<h3 data-start="145" data-end="197"><strong data-start="149" data-end="197">1. Classic VT100 (Terminal Green Monochrome)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="198" data-end="280"><strong data-start="198" data-end="214">Inspiration:</strong> 1970s–early 1980s text terminals (DEC VT100, Lear Siegler ADM).</p>
<p data-start="282" data-end="297"><strong data-start="282" data-end="297">Look &amp; Feel</strong></p>
<ul data-start="298" data-end="715">
<li data-start="298" data-end="329">
<p data-start="300" data-end="329">Pure black background <code data-start="322" data-end="328">#000</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="330" data-end="406">
<p data-start="332" data-end="406">Single phosphor-green color (<code data-start="361" data-end="370">#00FF00</code> / <code data-start="373" data-end="379">#0F0</code>) for all text and lines.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="407" data-end="495">
<p data-start="409" data-end="495">Slight blur or scanline effect, no animation except an optional text cursor flicker.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="496" data-end="576">
<p data-start="498" data-end="576">Interface feels <em data-start="514" data-end="533">command-line-like</em>: rectangular boxes drawn in ASCII style.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="577" data-end="632">
<p data-start="579" data-end="632">Fonts: monospaced (e.g., IBM Plex Mono, Fira Mono).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="633" data-end="715">
<p data-start="635" data-end="715">Minimal glow; evokes a <strong data-start="658" data-end="681">technical prototype</strong> or “digital lab notebook” feel.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="717" data-end="914"><strong data-start="717" data-end="730">Tone fit:</strong><br data-start="730" data-end="733">
Good if you want this site to feel like a <em data-start="775" data-end="793">research console</em> — precise, subdued, serious, and compatible with your other theoretical tools (RSVP simulator, HYDRA dashboard, etc.).</p>
<hr data-start="916" data-end="919">
<h3 data-start="921" data-end="990"><strong data-start="925" data-end="990">2. Vector-Monitor Arcade (1980s Asteroids / Battlezone Style)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="991" data-end="1069"><strong data-start="991" data-end="1007">Inspiration:</strong> Vector arcade games and oscilloscopic UIs (Atari, Vectrex).</p>
<p data-start="1071" data-end="1086"><strong data-start="1071" data-end="1086">Look &amp; Feel</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1087" data-end="1526">
<li data-start="1087" data-end="1200">
<p data-start="1089" data-end="1200">Still dark background, but lines and text <strong data-start="1131" data-end="1158">glow neon green or cyan</strong> with soft bloom and slight motion blur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1201" data-end="1261">
<p data-start="1203" data-end="1261">Subtle animated flicker or wave to simulate CRT refresh.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1262" data-end="1346">
<p data-start="1264" data-end="1346">Add optional color accents (amber, magenta highlights) for buttons or gridlines.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1347" data-end="1439">
<p data-start="1349" data-end="1439">Interface feels more <em data-start="1370" data-end="1381">cinematic</em> — luminous outlines, floating panels, scanline overlay.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1440" data-end="1526">
<p data-start="1442" data-end="1526">Fonts: thin geometric monospaced sans (e.g., Share Tech Mono, Major Mono Display).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1528" data-end="1722"><strong data-start="1528" data-end="1541">Tone fit:</strong><br data-start="1541" data-end="1544">
Good if you want the project to echo your <strong data-start="1586" data-end="1614">Flyxion vector aesthetic</strong> — artistic, immersive, and visually coherent with your other “Entropy’s Edge” and “RSVP cockpit” visuals.</p>
