p">Below is a **complete review of the new “Terminal” UI** together with **concrete, copy-and-paste-ready improvements** that raise robustness, accessibility, performance, and future-proofness while keeping the single-file, client-side spirit.

---

## 1. QUICK-WIN UI / UX FIXES  

| # | Problem | Fix (one-liner) | Why |
|---|---------|----------------|-----|
|1|<code>&lt;input id="scanInput"&gt;</code> is hidden inside the drop-zone text|Add <code>style="opacity:0;position:absolute;width:100%;height:100%;cursor:pointer;"</code>|Users can still click “choose file”|
|2|<code>processScans($("#scanInput").files)</code> is called from both button and drop|Pass <code>files</code> directly → avoid stale <code>FileList</code>|Prevents “no images selected” after drag-and-drop|
|3|Keyboard shortcuts fire on **any** focused input|Guard with <code>if (document.activeElement.tagName === 'BODY')</code>|Stops <code>R</code> from erasing a text field|
|4|Console overflows → scroll-jank|Add <code>scroll-behavior:smooth;</code> and limit height|<code>console { max-height:160px; overflow-y:auto; }</code>|
|5|No visual feedback while processing|Show spinner inside the **Process** button|<code>&lt;span id="procSpin" style="display:none"&gt;…&lt;/span&gt;</code>|

