<h3 data-start="915" data-end="961">🔍 <strong data-start="922" data-end="961">New: OpenCV.js Loader + Deskew Stub</strong></h3>
<p data-start="962" data-end="1016">Adds an <em data-start="970" data-end="980">optional</em> “Auto-Deskew (OpenCV)” button that:</p>
<ol data-start="1017" data-end="1276">
<li data-start="1017" data-end="1074">
<p data-start="1020" data-end="1074">Dynamically loads OpenCV.js (~1 MB, only on demand).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1075" data-end="1147">
<p data-start="1078" data-end="1147">Finds the four corner fiducials (<code data-start="1111" data-end="1143">cv.findContours → approxPolyDP</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1148" data-end="1276">
<p data-start="1151" data-end="1276">Applies <code data-start="1159" data-end="1189">cv.getPerspectiveTransform()</code> + <code data-start="1192" data-end="1214">cv.warpPerspective()</code><br data-start="1214" data-end="1217">
to deskew the scanned image before glyph segmentation.</p>
</li>
</ol>
