<li data-start="115" data-end="372">
<p data-start="118" data-end="192">Include the <strong data-start="130" data-end="162">compiled PDF (<code data-start="146" data-end="159">xenobot.pdf</code>)</strong> alongside the LaTeX source.</p>
<ul data-start="196" data-end="372">
<li data-start="196" data-end="276">
<p data-start="198" data-end="276">If it can be generated cleanly during packaging, it will be inside <code data-start="265" data-end="273">paper/</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="280" data-end="372">
<p data-start="282" data-end="372">If it can’t, you’ll still have the full TeX + workflow to rebuild automatically on push.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="373" data-end="511">
<p data-start="376" data-end="511">Embed all simulators (Xenobot Swarm v2.1 + Stars! RSVP v1.0 + v2.0) fully contained—no external dependencies except CDN JS libraries.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="512" data-end="613">
<p data-start="515" data-end="613">Add a unified <code data-start="529" data-end="540">README.md</code> that links theory (RSVP) → simulation → paper → GitHub Pages deployment.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="615" data-end="618">
<p data-start="620" data-end="685">Once done, you’ll get a <strong data-start="644" data-end="672">ready-to-publish archive</strong> that can be:</p>
<ul data-start="686" data-end="843">
<li data-start="686" data-end="753">
<p data-start="688" data-end="753">Unzipped and opened locally (simulators run instantly in browser)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="754" data-end="806">
<p data-start="756" data-end="806">Pushed directly to GitHub (autobuilds PDF + Pages)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="807" data-end="843">
<p data-start="809" data-end="843">Extended for further RSVP research</p>
</li>
</ul>
